                <pb facs="0821" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11698: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ballantine</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-31T11:00:00+08:00">December 31, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 31—2:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have just been informed authoritatively that the necessary order for the
                    dissolution of the National Government at Canton on January 1st is being issued
                    today.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking, Legation at Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ballantine</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
